tes on each side. Drain on paper towels. Garnish with strips of smoked salmon and pickled ginger, and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 179.0, "protein_g": 3.2, "carbohydrates_g": 5.4, "fat_g": 16.9, "saturated_fat_g": 1.8, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 20.0, "sodium_mg": 154.9, "fiber_g": 1.2, "sugar_g": 0.9, "unsaturated_fat_g": 14.5, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["jewish"], "diet": [], "course": [], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": ["hanukkah"], "other": ["fry", "mushroom", "pecan", "winter"]}, "images": [], "rating": null, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1998-12-16", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:02:23.323155+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "mushroom-pozole-rojo", "nyt_id": 776107079, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/776107079-mushroom-pozole-rojo", "name": "Mushroom Pozole Rojo", "author": "Paola Briseño-González", "description": "Mushroom pozole has long been the vegetarian anchor of pozole tables across Mexico, sturdy and deliciously satisfying. Start by browning the mushrooms to build serious flavor. The jamminess of guajillo chiles and the raisin-like flavor of ancho help build a broth that’s complex, velvety and quietly intense. A can of hominy keeps this within reach on a weeknight, but dried hominy, soaked overnight and simmered until each kernel blooms open like popcorn, gives the most tender chew — see Tip for instructions. If you spot refrigerated pre-cooked hominy at a Latin market, grab it (the texture is very similar to freshly cooked). Ladle this pozole rojo steaming into shallow bowls and pile on the contrast: crisp shreds of iceberg lettuce, a generous squeeze of lime and thin radish coins for a peppery snap. It’s exactly the kind of bowl that makes you feel warm and revived.", "servings": {"text": "6-8 servings", "min": 6, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 10, "cook_minutes": 90, "total_minutes": 100, "raw": {"total": "1 hr 40 min", "prep": "PT0H10M", "cook": "PT1H30M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 ounce dried red guajillo chiles (4 to 5 large chiles)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "dried red guajillo chiles (4 to 5 large chiles)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "½ ounce ancho chiles (2 to 3 medium chiles)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "ancho chiles (2 to 3 medium chiles)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 medium tomato (about 8 ounces)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium tomato (about 8 ounces)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "½ medium white onion, plus ½ cup finely chopped (for garnish)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium white onion", "preparation": "plus ½ cup finely chopped (for garnish)", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 large garlic cloves, peeled", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large garlic cloves", "preparation": "peeled", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 tablespoon extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 pounds white button or cremini mushrooms, tough stems removed, thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "white button or cremini mushrooms", "preparation": "tough stems removed, thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1½ teaspoons dried Mexican oregano, plus more dried oregano for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "½ teaspoons dried mexican oregano", "preparation": "plus more dried oregano for garnish", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 quart low-sodium vegetable broth", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "quart", "item": "low-sodium vegetable broth", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 bay leaf", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "bay leaf", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "1 (29-ounce) can cooked hominy, drained and rinsed", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "(29-ounce) can cooked hominy", "preparation": "drained and rinsed", "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "Lime wedges, for serving", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "lime wedges", "preparation": "for serving", "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "Thinly sliced iceberg lettuce, for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "thinly sliced iceberg lettuce", "preparation": "for garnish", "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "Thinly sliced radishes, for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "thinly sliced radishes", "preparation": "for garnish", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a dry medium cast-iron skillet or comal over medium-high heat, lightly toast the dried chiles, turning them often with tongs so they don't burn, until fragrant and blackened in spots, 3 to 5 minutes. Wearing gloves, cut chiles lengthwise with kitchen shears or a paring knife. Remove and discard stems and seeds."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a medium saucepan, combine the chiles with the tomato, onion half and garlic, and fill the pot with water to cover. Bring to a boil on high, then turn off heat and cover the pot. Let stand until chiles are softened and pulpy, 5 to 10 minutes. Using a slotted spoon, transfer the solids to a blender (discard soaking liquid). Add 2 cups water to the blender and purée to a smooth paste. Set chile paste aside."}, {"position": 3, "text": "In a large Dutch oven or other heavy-bottomed pot, heat oil over medium-high. Add mushrooms and oregano, and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened and all the liquid has evaporated, 10 minutes. Season with salt and pepper. Continue to cook, stirring occasionally, until mushrooms are lightly browned, 5 more minutes. Add the broth, 4 cups water and the bay leaf. Bring to a boil, stirring to scrape any browned bits from the bottom of the pot. Cover, reduce the heat to low, and cook, stirring occasionally, 10 minutes."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Uncover the pot and remove the bay leaf. Stir the reserved chile purée through a fine-mesh sieve into the pot, pressing down with a spoon (discard solids). Add hominy to the pot and adjust the heat to a simmer to allow the flavors to come together, 10 minutes. Taste and adjust seasoning. Let pozole stand for 10 minutes before serving."}, {"position": 5, "text": "To serve, ladle pozole into wide bowls. Serve alongside bowls of chopped onion, lime wedges, lettuce, radishes and dried oregano for garnishing as you please. (Pozole can be cooled completely and reheated later. Refrigerate for up to 3 days.)"}], "nutrition": {"calories": 134.6, "protein_g": 5.2, "carbohydrates_g": 24.1, "fat_g": 3.0, "saturated_fat_g": 0.4, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 866.1, "fiber_g": 4.7, "sugar_g": 4.8, "unsaturated_fat_g": 2.3, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["mexican"], "diet": ["dairy-free", "gluten-free", "healthy", "vegan", "vegetarian"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner", "breakfast", "lunch"], "occasion": ["party"], "other": ["guajillo chile", "ancho chile", "soup", "vegetables", "simmer", "stovetop", "make-ahead", "great leftovers", "cremini", "white mushroom", "budget", "spring", "fall"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/04/14/multimedia/PBG-Mushroom-Pozole-vchp/PBG-Mushroom-Pozole-vchp-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 24}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2026-04-14", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:26:30.131202+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "mushroom-ragout", "nyt_id": 11651, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11651-mushroom-ragout", "name": "Mushroom Ragout", "author": "Nigella Lawson", "description": "Nigella Lawson brought this recipe to The Times in a 2006 article about vegetarian comfort food. \"The mushrooms, which are easy to cook, require a certain amount of patience and trust. Once you tumble your huge pile of prepared mushrooms into the pan, you could quite reasonably believe they will never cook down, never lose their bouncy rawness and could go on absorbing oil forever. Just start by moving them around gingerly in the pan and then, when they have all had their turn in the heat, clamp on a lid and let them give off their bosky juices.\" Serve with Ms. Lawson's Spiced and Herbed Millet (as shown) or rice.", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 55, "raw": {"total": "55 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 ounce dried porcini mushrooms", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "dried porcini mushrooms", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 pounds mixed fresh mushrooms (like button, cremini, chanterelle, oyster)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "mixed fresh mushrooms (like button", "preparation": "cremini, chanterelle, oyster)", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "¼ cup olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 onion, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "onion", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "3 garlic cloves, peeled and finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "peeled and finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 teaspoon ground cumin", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground cumin", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 teaspoon celery salt", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "celery salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "2 tablespoons flour", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "¼ cup Amontillado or cream sherry", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "amontillado or cream sherry", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "Finely grated zest of half a lemon", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "finely grated zest of half a lemon", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "2 tablespoons chopped parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Soak porcini in 1 ½ cups boiling water until softened, at least 20 minutes. Pick over fresh mushrooms, tearing or slicing bigger ones as needed."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Place a large sauté pan over medium heat and add olive oil. Add onion and garlic and sauté until softened. Stir in cumin and celery salt. Drain porcini, reserving liquid, and add to pan, stirring for 1 to 2 minutes."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Add fresh mushrooms and turn in pan until they begin to soften. Cover and cook, stirring occasionally, for 5 minutes."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Stir in flour, followed by porcini soaking liquid and sherry. Cover and simmer until mushrooms are cooked through but retain a meaty bite, about 20 minutes. Transfer to a warmed platter, and sprinkle with a mixture of lemon zest and parsley. Serve with millet (as shown) or rice."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 157.6, "protein_g": 5.9, "carbohydrates_g": 14.3, "fat_g": 9.7, "saturated_fat_g": 1.4, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 11.3, "fiber_g": 2.7, "sugar_g": 4.5, "unsaturated_fat_g": 7.9, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["vegetarian"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["fall", "mushroom", "saute", "winter"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/06/03/dining/Ragout/Ragout-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 346}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2006-03-01", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:48:37.192513+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "mussel-stuffed-flounder-fillets-with-vegetables-and-mussel-broth", "nyt_id": 10960, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10960-mussel-stuffed-flounder-fillets-with-vegetables-and-mussel-broth", "name": "Mussel-Stuffed Flounder Fillets With Vegetables And Mussel Broth", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "Four servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 60, "raw": {"total": "About 1 hour"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "Ingredients for steamed mussels (see recipe)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "ingredients for steamed mussels (see recipe)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "16 mussels", "group": null, "quantity": 16.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "mussels", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 8-ounce flounder fillets, split lengthwise", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "8-ounce flounder fillets", "preparation": "split lengthwise", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 teaspoons salt, plus more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": "plus more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 teaspoons olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 medium onion, peeled and cut into small dice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium onion", "preparation": "peeled and cut into small dice", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "3 medium carrots, peeled and cut into small dice", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium carrots", "preparation": "peeled and cut into small dice", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 large baking potatoes, peeled and very thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large baking potatoes", "preparation": "peeled and very thinly sliced", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Steam the mussels (see recipe). Reserve the broth. Remove the mussels from their shells and halve them if large. Lay the flounder on a work surface, skin side up. Season with 1 teaspoon salt and some pepper. Lay 4 mussels (or 8 halves) on each piece of fillet and roll it up like a jellyroll. Set aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Heat the olive oil in a large saucepan over low heat. Add the onion and carrots, and cook until softened, about 15 minutes. Measure the mussel broth and add enough water to equal 1 ½ cups. Stir in 1 teaspoon salt. Layer the potato slices over the onions and carrots, add the broth and bring to a boil. Reduce to a simmer, cover and cook for 12 minutes. Place the flounder rolls on top of the potatoes, cover and cook until fish is just cooked through, about 10 minutes."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Carefully place 1 flounder roll in each of 4 soup plates. Divide the vegetables among the plates, arranging them around the fish. Ladle the broth over and serve immediately."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 13.3, "protein_g": 1.1, "carbohydrates_g": 1.7, "fat_g": 0.2, "saturated_fat_g": 0.0, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 2.8, "sodium_mg": 40.8, "fiber_g": 0.2, "sugar_g": 0.2, "unsaturated_fat_g": 0.2, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["gluten-free"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["boil", "flounder", "mussel"]}, "images": [], 